# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. The model and the physics {#1-the-model-and-the-physics}"
msgstr "1. Ang model at ang physics {#1-the-model-and-the-physics}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$H = -t \\sum_{\\langle ij\\rangle} \\left(b_i^\\dagger b_j + b_j^\\dagger b_i\\right), \\qquad (b_i^\\dagger)^2 = 0 .$$\n"
msgstr "$$H = -t \\sum_{\\langle ij\\rangle} \\left(b_i^\\dagger b_j + b_j^\\dagger b_i\\right), \\qquad (b_i^\\dagger)^2 = 0 .$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this model, bosons hop between neighboring sites $\\langle ij\\rangle$ of a square lattice. In principle, a site can hold any number of bosons; however,\n"
"**hard-core** bosons are forbidden to share a site. Thus, every site holds either zero or one boson. In `qiskit-bosons`, that is handled through the\n"
"truncation $d = 2$ (`max_occupation = 1`) during the boson-to-qubit mapping. Each site is then mapped as a two-level system and the model is the spin-1/2 XY model,\n"
"$b_i^\\dagger b_j + \\mathrm{h.c.} = \\tfrac12(X_iX_j + Y_iY_j)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa model na ito, lumilipat ang mga boson sa pagitan ng magkakatabing site na $\\langle ij\\rangle$ ng isang square lattice. Sa prinsipyo, maaaring maglaman ang isang site ng kahit ilang boson; gayunpaman, ipinagbabawal sa **hard-core** bosons na magsalo sa isang site. Kaya, bawat site ay may laman na zero o isang boson. Sa `qiskit-bosons`, hinahawakan ito sa pamamagitan ng\n"
"truncation na $d = 2$ (`max_occupation = 1`) sa boson-to-qubit mapping. Ang bawat site ay imamapa bilang two-level system at ang model ay ang spin-1/2 XY model,\n"
"$b_i^\\dagger b_j + \\mathrm{h.c.} = \\tfrac12(X_iX_j + Y_iY_j)$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**How this relates to the Bose-Hubbard model.** Bose-Hubbard adds an on-site repulsion $\\tfrac U2 n_i(n_i-1)$ to the hopping\n"
"term, which penalizes two bosons on one site. Hard-core is the limit $U \\to \\infty$, where double occupation is forbidden\n"
"outright. In the truncated space $n_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}$, $n_i(n_i-1) = 0$, so the on-site term vanishes whatever $U$ is\n"
"and the Hamiltonian has no interaction parameter at all. Note that this is the opposite of $U = 0$, which is the free\n"
"boson, where a site can hold many bosons.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Paano ito nauugnay sa Bose-Hubbard model.** Nagdaragdag ang Bose-Hubbard ng on-site repulsion na $\\tfrac U2 n_i(n_i-1)$ sa hopping\n"
"term, na pumaparusa sa dalawang boson sa isang site. Ang hard-core ay ang limit na $U \\to \\infty$, kung saan\n"
"tuluyang ipinagbabawal ang double occupation. Sa truncated na space na $n_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}$, $n_i(n_i-1) = 0$, kaya nawawala ang on-site term anuman ang $U$\n"
"at walang interaction parameter ang Hamiltonian. Tandaan na ito ang kabaligtaran ng $U = 0$, ang free\n"
"boson, kung saan maaaring maglaman ang isang site ng maraming boson.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Why 1D is classically easy and 2D is not.** On an open chain, hard-core bosons are exactly free fermions: the Jordan-Wigner\n"
"transformation turns the spin chain into a quadratic fermion Hamiltonian with no string left over, because particles\n"
"cannot hop past each other. On a grid, a hop around a plaquette exchanges particles, and the sign that the fermions would pick up\n"
"is not matched by the bosons. The cells below check this with `qiskit-fermions`: they build free fermions that hop on the same\n"
"bonds, map them with `jordan_wigner` (qubit $j$ is mode $j$, sites numbered row by row) and compare the spectra with\n"
"the hard-core Hamiltonian in every particle-number sector. The hard-core matrix itself is built with plain numpy, because\n"
"it is a boson model.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kung bakit madali ang 1D sa classical na paraan at hindi ang 2D.** Sa isang open chain, ang hard-core bosons ay eksaktong free fermions: ang Jordan-Wigner\n"
"transformation ay ginagawang quadratic fermion Hamiltonian ang spin chain na walang natitirang string, dahil hindi\n"
"makakalundag ang mga particle sa isa't isa. Sa isang grid, ang pag-hop sa paligid ng plaquette ay nagpapalit ng mga particle, at ang sign na makukuha ng mga fermion\n"
"ay hindi tugma sa mga boson. Sinusuri ito ng mga cell sa ibaba gamit ang `qiskit-fermions`: bumubuo sila ng free fermions na naghe-hop sa parehong\n"
"mga bond, ima-map ang mga ito gamit ang `jordan_wigner` (ang qubit $j$ ay mode $j$, ang mga site ay binibilang row by row) at inihahambing ang mga spectrum sa\n"
"hard-core Hamiltonian sa bawat particle-number sector. Ang hard-core matrix mismo ay binubuo gamit ang payak na numpy, dahil\n"
"isa itong boson model.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the open chain, the two Hamiltonians are the same matrix and the spectra agree to rounding in every sector. On the grids,\n"
"they differ at order one, and the ring with an even particle number fails too, because particles can circle around it. So the\n"
"1D case is classically easy (free fermions are a polynomial problem) and the 2D case is the interesting one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa open chain, iisang matrix ang dalawang Hamiltonian at nagtutugma ang mga spectrum hanggang sa rounding sa bawat sector. Sa mga grid,\n"
"magkaiba sila sa order one, at pumapalya rin ang ring na may even na bilang ng particle, dahil maaaring umikot ang mga particle dito. Kaya\n"
"madali sa classical na paraan ang 1D na kaso (ang free fermions ay isang polynomial na problema) at ang 2D na kaso ang kawili-wili.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Build the `BosonicCircuit` {#2-build-the-bosoniccircuit}"
msgstr "2. Buuin ang `BosonicCircuit` {#2-build-the-bosoniccircuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A hopping term is Hermitian only together with its conjugate pair, so both stay in one group. Bonds that share no site commute, so an\n"
"**edge coloring** of the square lattice gives groups that commute internally at the bosonic level:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang hopping term ay Hermitian lamang kasama ng conjugate pair nito, kaya nananatili ang dalawa sa isang group. Ang mga bond na walang pinagsasaluhang site ay nagko-commute, kaya ang\n"
"**edge coloring** ng square lattice ay nagbibigay ng mga group na nagko-commute sa loob sa bosonic na antas:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "color 0 / 1: horizontal bonds starting at an even / odd column (blue pair)\n"
msgstr "color 0 / 1: mga pahalang na bond na nagsisimula sa even / odd na column (asul na pares)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "color 2 / 3: vertical bonds starting at an even / odd row (orange and red)\n"
msgstr "color 2 / 3: mga patayong bond na nagsisimula sa even / odd na row (orange at pula)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two bonds of the same color never share a site, because the bonds along a line alternate colors. The construction below takes\n"
"only the lattice size $(L_x, L_y)$ as input, and everything after it (circuit, encoding, transpilation) is identical for every\n"
"size. The drawing shows the site numbering ($s = L_x y + x$) and the colors for a $4\\times4$ lattice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang dalawang bond na may parehong color ay hindi kailanman nagsasalo ng site, dahil nag-aalternate ang mga color ng mga bond sa isang linya. Ang construction sa ibaba ay kumukuha\n"
"ng laki ng lattice lang na $(L_x, L_y)$ bilang input, at ang lahat ng kasunod nito (circuit, encoding, transpilation) ay magkapareho para sa bawat\n"
"laki. Ipinapakita ng drawing ang pagnunumero ng site ($s = L_x y + x$) at ang mga color para sa $4\\times4$ na lattice.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/57d33dfd-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/57d33dfd-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run some simple checks of the construction on a few lattices: every color group is Hermitian, and the bonds of a color are site-disjoint (so each group commutes internally).\n"
msgstr "Magpatakbo ng ilang simpleng check sa construction sa ilang lattice: Hermitian ang bawat color group, at site-disjoint ang mga bond ng isang color (kaya nagko-commute sa loob ang bawat group).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now construct the circuit. The whole Trotter step is **one** `Evolution` gate over all modes. `BosonicLieTrotter` decides how it splits,\n"
"and one `decompose()` shows the split: one `Evolution` per color and per Trotter step. The circuit mentions neither the\n"
"truncation nor the encoding; those come in when the transpiler preset lowers it to qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon, buuin ang circuit. Ang buong Trotter step ay **isang** `Evolution` gate sa lahat ng mode. Ang `BosonicLieTrotter` ang nagpapasya kung paano ito hahatiin,\n"
"at ipinapakita ng isang `decompose()` ang paghahati: isang `Evolution` bawat color at bawat Trotter step. Hindi binabanggit ng circuit ang\n"
"truncation o ang encoding; papasok ang mga iyon kapag ibinaba ito ng transpiler preset sa mga qubit.\n"

