# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ENCODINGS`: the four `LevelEncoding`s that map a boson mode with $d$ levels to qubits. At $d = 2$, the\n"
"standard-binary and Gray codes are the same code with one qubit per mode (qubit $= $ occupation), while the two unary codes use one qubit per level (two qubits per mode) and differ only in whether they project onto the valid unary states.\n"
msgstr ""
"`ENCODINGS`: ang apat na `LevelEncoding` na nagma-map ng boson mode na may $d$ na level sa mga qubit. Sa $d = 2$, ang\n"
"standard-binary at Gray code ay iisang code na may isang qubit bawat mode (qubit $= $ occupation), habang ang dalawang unary code ay gumagamit ng isang qubit bawat level (dalawang qubit bawat mode) at nagkakaiba lang sa kung magpo-project ba sila sa mga valid na unary state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`BASIS`: the hardware gate set used for counting (`cz`, `rz`, `sx`, `x`).\n"
