# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Compute a Néel quench {#3-compute-a-néel-quench}"
msgstr "3. Kwentahin ang isang Néel quench {#3-compute-a-néel-quench}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can now watch the bosons move under a quench. The dynamics start from a **Néel pattern**: the sites of a checkerboard are alternately\n"
"filled with one boson (black circles in the drawing below) and empty (white circles), so half of the sites are occupied. At\n"
"time zero, the state is a single bit string, which is easy to prepare (one `X` gate per occupied site). It is not an eigenstate of\n"
"the hopping Hamiltonian: every bond of the lattice joins an occupied and an empty site, so every bond can move a boson,\n"
"and the state starts to change right away. Preparing a simple state and then letting it evolve under a Hamiltonian that it\n"
"is not an eigenstate of is called a **quench**.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mo nang panoorin ang paggalaw ng mga boson sa ilalim ng quench. Nagsisimula ang dynamics sa isang **Néel pattern**: salitang pinupunan ang mga site ng checkerboard\n"
"ng isang boson (mga itim na bilog sa drawing sa ibaba) at iniiwang walang laman (mga puting bilog), kaya kalahati ng mga site ang may laman. Sa\n"
"oras na zero, ang state ay isang bit string lang, na madaling ihanda (isang `X` gate bawat site na may laman). Hindi ito eigenstate ng\n"
"hopping Hamiltonian: ang bawat bond ng lattice ay nagdudugtong ng site na may laman at walang laman, kaya kayang ilipat ng bawat bond ang isang boson,\n"
"at agad na nagsisimulang magbago ang state. Ang paghahanda ng simpleng state at pagpapaiwas dito na mag-evolve sa ilalim ng Hamiltonian na hindi\n"
"nito eigenstate ay tinatawag na **quench**.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/d8ccb302-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/d8ccb302-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because the lattice is bipartite, a hop always moves a boson to the other sublattice of the checkerboard. This suggests the\n"
"observable to follow, the **staggered density imbalance**\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil bipartite ang lattice, laging inililipat ng hop ang boson sa kabilang sublattice ng checkerboard. Iminumungkahi nito ang\n"
"observable na susundan, ang **staggered density imbalance**\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\mathcal I(t) = \\frac1N \\sum_i (-1)^{x_i+y_i}\\,\\bigl(2\\langle n_i\\rangle(t) - 1\\bigr) = \\frac{2}{N}\\bigl(N_A(t) - N_B(t)\\bigr),$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\mathcal I(t) = \\frac1N \\sum_i (-1)^{x_i+y_i}\\,\\bigl(2\\langle n_i\\rangle(t) - 1\\bigr) = \\frac{2}{N}\\bigl(N_A(t) - N_B(t)\\bigr),$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $N_A$ and $N_B$ are the numbers of bosons on the two sublattices. It measures how many bosons are still on the\n"
"sublattice they started on. It starts at $\\mathcal I = 1$ and, as the bosons spread over the lattice, falls and then\n"
"fluctuates around zero, where neither sublattice is preferred. On hardware, it is cheap to measure, because it only needs\n"
"the occupation of each site, that is, single-qubit $Z$ measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $N_A$ at $N_B$ ay ang bilang ng mga boson sa dalawang sublattice. Sinusukat nito kung ilang boson ang nasa\n"
"sublattice pa rin na pinagsimulan nila. Nagsisimula ito sa $\\mathcal I = 1$ at, habang kumakalat ang mga boson sa lattice, bumababa at pagkatapos ay\n"
"umiikot sa paligid ng zero, kung saan walang sublattice na pinapaboran. Sa hardware, mura itong sukatin, dahil kailangan lang nito\n"
"ang occupation ng bawat site, ibig sabihin, mga single-qubit na $Z$ measurement.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The later plots of the observable behavior also show the density of individual sites.\n"
"In one dimension, this quench is a free-fermion problem, but on a square lattice it is not (as discussed in section 1), so the exact evolution of the $4\\times4$ lattice below is the reference. The hard-core Hilbert space is the set of bit strings, and $b_i^\\dagger b_j$ moves a bit. Build $H$ as a sparse matrix with plain numpy and evolve with `expm_multiply`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapakita rin ng mga susunod na plot ng behavior ng observable ang density ng mga indibidwal na site.\n"
"Sa isang dimensyon, ang quench na ito ay isang free-fermion na problema, pero sa square lattice ay hindi (gaya ng tinalakay sa seksyon 1), kaya ang eksaktong evolution ng $4\\times4$ na lattice sa ibaba ang reference. Ang hard-core Hilbert space ay ang set ng mga bit string, at ang $b_i^\\dagger b_j$ ay naglilipat ng isang bit. Buuin ang $H$ bilang sparse matrix gamit ang payak na numpy at i-evolve gamit ang `expm_multiply`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, compute the exact reference.\n"
msgstr "Una, kwentahin ang eksaktong reference.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, check the `InitializeModes` gate, which also confirms that the mode-to-qubit encoding is correct.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, suriin ang `InitializeModes` gate, na kumukumpirma rin na tama ang mode-to-qubit encoding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now compute the Trotterized curves. A circuit is one first-order Trotter step of length $dt$ (all four colors once), applied\n"
"$T/dt$ times; `trotter_series` returns the site densities at every multiple of $dt$. The cell after it turns the densities of\n"
"the exact and of the Trotterized evolution into the three observables to plot.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon, kwentahin ang mga Trotterized na curve. Ang isang circuit ay isang first-order na Trotter step na may haba na $dt$ (lahat ng apat na color nang isang beses), na ina-apply\n"
"nang $T/dt$ na beses; ibinabalik ng `trotter_series` ang mga site density sa bawat multiple ng $dt$. Ang cell pagkatapos nito ay ginagawang tatlong observable na iplot ang mga density ng\n"
"eksaktong evolution at ng Trotterized na evolution.\n"

