# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Beyond hard-core bosons: higher mode truncation {#7-beyond-hard-core-bosons-higher-mode-truncation}"
msgstr "7. Higit pa sa hard-core bosons: mas mataas na mode truncation {#7-beyond-hard-core-bosons-higher-mode-truncation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Everything so far only considered hard-core bosons, so the on-site term could not act. With $d = 3$, a site can\n"
"hold two bosons, $\\tfrac U2 n(n-1)$ appears as a third group (diagonal), and the hopping matrix elements acquire $\\sqrt2$ factors.\n"
"The next cell builds the Bose-Hubbard step on a 4-site chain and measures its cost the same way, for all four encodings, next to the hard-core chain of the same length.\n"
msgstr "Hanggang ngayon, hard-core bosons lang ang isinaalang-alang, kaya hindi makakilos ang on-site term. Sa $d = 3$, ang isang site ay maaaring maglaman ng dalawang boson, lumilitaw ang $\\tfrac U2 n(n-1)$ bilang ikatlong group (diagonal), at nagkakaroon ng mga factor na $\\sqrt2$ ang mga hopping matrix element. Binubuo ng susunod na cell ang Bose-Hubbard step sa isang 4-site na chain at sinusukat ang gastos nito sa parehong paraan, para sa lahat ng apat na encoding, katabi ng hard-core chain na may parehong haba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The physics becomes significantly more complicated and the favorable scaling disappears.\n"
msgstr "Nagiging mas masalimuot ang physics at naglalaho ang paborableng scaling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial used hard-core bosons because they make for simple analyses while emphasizing the benefits of the `qiskit-bosons` package and architecture of its transpiler framework. It is set up to investigate real bosonic physics beyond such simple truncation limits, but exploring these circuits and researching their application is now up to you.\n"
msgstr "Gumamit ng hard-core bosons ang tutorial na ito dahil nagiging simple ang mga analysis habang idinidiin ang mga benepisyo ng `qiskit-bosons` package at ng arkitektura ng transpiler framework nito. Nakahanda itong mag-imbestiga ng totoong bosonic physics na lampas sa ganitong simpleng truncation limit, ngunit nasa iyo na ngayon ang paggalugad sa mga Circuit na ito at pag-research sa kanilang aplikasyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "8. Takeaways and next steps {#8-takeaways-and-next-steps}"
msgstr "8. Mga takeaway at susunod na hakbang {#8-takeaways-and-next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The output below recaps the circuit cost of a single Trotter step for the hard-core lattices, and the Trotter error of the small system.\n"
msgstr "Ibinubuod ng output sa ibaba ang gastos ng Circuit ng isang Trotter step para sa mga hard-core lattice, at ang Trotter error ng maliit na system.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From these numbers, you can draw some high-level takeaways. The first ones are about the framework, which is what you\n"
"carry over to other bosonic models. The later ones are about what the results show for hard-core bosons, the simple test case.\n"
msgstr "Mula sa mga numerong ito, makakakuha ka ng ilang high-level na takeaway. Ang mga una ay tungkol sa framework, na siyang dadalhin mo sa iba pang bosonic model. Ang mga huli ay tungkol sa ipinapakita ng mga resulta para sa hard-core bosons, ang simpleng test case.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A framework for bosonic physics.** `qiskit-bosons` separates three things: the model (a `BosonOperator`, grouped here\n"
"by edge color), the circuit (one `Evolution` gate and a Trotter formula that splits it), and the lowering to qubits (the mode\n"
"truncation $d$ and the `LevelEncoding`, chosen when the transpiler preset runs). Changing one of them leaves the other two\n"
"untouched (sections 2 and 7).\n"
msgstr "**Isang framework para sa bosonic physics.** Pinaghihiwalay ng `qiskit-bosons` ang tatlong bagay: ang modelo (isang `BosonOperator`, na dito ay naka-group ayon sa edge color), ang Circuit (isang `Evolution` gate at isang Trotter formula na naghahati rito), at ang lowering sa mga qubit (ang mode truncation $d$ at ang `LevelEncoding`, na pinipili kapag tumakbo ang transpiler preset). Ang pagbabago sa isa sa mga ito ay hindi nakakaapekto sa dalawa pa (seksyon 2 at 7).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Why Trotterize at the bosonic level.** The grouping lives in the operator, so the Trotter circuit comes out with a flat depth\n"
"without any ordering by hand. One `PauliEvolutionGate` over the same qubit operator has the same Trotter error order and\n"
"scaling, and with the terms sorted by color it is the identical circuit. In another order, the depth grows with the lattice\n"
"(84 against 8 for one first-order step at $10\\times12$) or the gate count is about a third higher (sections 4 and 5).\n"
msgstr "**Bakit mag-Trotterize sa bosonic level.** Nasa operator ang grouping, kaya lumalabas ang Trotter Circuit na may flat na depth nang walang anumang mano-manong pag-aayos ng pagkakasunod. Ang isang `PauliEvolutionGate` sa parehong qubit operator ay may parehong Trotter error order at scaling, at kapag nakaayos ang mga term ayon sa kulay, magkapareho ang Circuit. Sa ibang pagkakasunod, lumalaki ang depth kasabay ng lattice (84 laban sa 8 para sa isang first-order step sa $10\\times12$) o humigit-kumulang isang katlo na mas mataas ang bilang ng gate (seksyon 4 at 5).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Accuracy.** The only numerical error is the Trotter error between the colors, and it falls with the number of steps as\n"
"expected for first and second order (section 4). The qubit side and the encoding add nothing.\n"
msgstr "**Katumpakan.** Ang tanging numerical error ay ang Trotter error sa pagitan ng mga kulay, at bumababa ito kasabay ng bilang ng step gaya ng inaasahan para sa first at second order (seksyon 4). Walang idinaragdag ang panig ng qubit at ang encoding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The encoding is a cost choice.** At $d = 2$, all four encodings give the same physics. The compact codes need half the\n"
"qubits and are about 20 times cheaper in depth and gates than the unary ones (section 5).\n"
msgstr "**Ang encoding ay pagpili ng gastos.** Sa $d = 2$, magkakapareho ang physics ng lahat ng apat na encoding. Kalahati lang ng mga qubit ang kailangan ng mga compact code at humigit-kumulang 20 beses na mas mura sa depth at gate kaysa sa mga unary (seksyon 5).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Hardware.** With the natural embedding of the lattice, every gate already sits on a Nighthawk coupler, so the chip runs the\n"
"circuit with no routing overhead at any size up to the whole chip (section 6).\n"
msgstr "**Hardware.** Sa natural na embedding ng lattice, nasa Nighthawk coupler na ang bawat gate, kaya pinapatakbo ng chip ang Circuit nang walang routing overhead sa anumang laki hanggang sa buong chip (seksyon 6).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **Hard-core bosons are the entry point, not the goal.** They are the $U\\to\\infty$ limit of Bose-Hubbard, with the XY model as\n"
"  a spin-1/2 equivalent. They are exactly free fermions on an open chain but not on a square lattice, which makes 2D the\n"
"  interesting case (section 1). Raising the truncation to $d = 3$ brings the on-site interaction back and the cost jumps (a\n"
"  4-site chain goes from a two-qubit depth of 4 to 95 in the Gray code, section 7). That is where the exploration of bosonic\n"
"  physics begins, and the same framework carries it.\n"
"**Caveats.** All depths are for a noise-free fake backend (`FakeNighthawk`) and one fixed basis (`cz, rz, sx, x`, optimization\n"
"level 3); they compare structure, not fidelity. The routed numbers equal the abstract ones only because the natural embedding\n"
"puts every gate on a coupler. The Néel quench is one initial state; the Trotter error depends on the state and on $T$. Nothing\n"
"here runs on real hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"* **Ang hard-core bosons ang panimulang punto, hindi ang layunin.** Ito ang $U\\to\\infty$ limit ng Bose-Hubbard, na may XY model bilang katumbas na spin-1/2. Eksakto silang mga free fermion sa isang open chain ngunit hindi sa square lattice, kaya ang 2D ang kawili-wiling kaso (seksyon 1). Ang pagtaas ng truncation sa $d = 3$ ay nagbabalik ng on-site interaction at tumataas nang husto ang gastos (ang isang 4-site na chain ay napupunta mula two-qubit depth na 4 tungo sa 95 sa Gray code, seksyon 7). Doon nagsisimula ang paggalugad ng bosonic physics, at dala ito ng parehong framework.\n"
"**Mga paalala.** Ang lahat ng depth ay para sa noise-free na fake Backend (`FakeNighthawk`) at isang nakapirming basis (`cz, rz, sx, x`, optimization level 3); naghahambing ang mga ito ng estruktura, hindi ng fidelity. Ang mga routed na numero ay katumbas ng mga abstract dahil lang inilalagay ng natural na embedding ang bawat gate sa isang coupler. Ang Néel quench ay isang initial state; nakadepende ang Trotter error sa state at sa $T$. Walang tumatakbo rito sa totoong hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Next steps.** Hard-core bosons are a simple, checkable model to learn the framework on. From here, the same building\n"
"blocks apply to the models that are hard to treat classically:\n"
msgstr "**Mga susunod na hakbang.** Ang hard-core bosons ay isang simple at masusuring modelo para pag-aralan ang framework. Mula rito, nalalapat ang parehong building block sa mga modelong mahirap gamutin nang klasikal:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Larger cutoffs $d$ (soft-core bosons, the full Bose-Hubbard model), where the choice of encoding and of Trotter formula\n"
"matters much more than here (section 7)\n"
msgstr "Mas malalaking cutoff na $d$ (soft-core bosons, ang buong Bose-Hubbard model), kung saan mas mahalaga ang pagpili ng encoding at ng Trotter formula kaysa rito (seksyon 7)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other Hamiltonians, such as bosons with a different interaction or a different coupling to their environment\n"
msgstr "Iba pang Hamiltonian, tulad ng mga boson na may ibang interaksyon o ibang coupling sa kanilang kapaligiran\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other lattices, such as triangular or honeycomb, which need other edge colorings and other hardware embeddings\n"
msgstr "Iba pang lattice, tulad ng triangular o honeycomb, na nangangailangan ng ibang edge coloring at ibang hardware embedding\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Correlation functions as observables, such as $\\langle X_iX_j + Y_iY_j\\rangle$ and density-density correlators\n"
msgstr "Mga correlation function bilang observable, tulad ng $\\langle X_iX_j + Y_iY_j\\rangle$ at density-density correlator\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mixed models (bosons coupled to fermions or to a bath)\n"
msgstr "Mga halo-halong modelo (mga boson na naka-couple sa mga fermion o sa isang bath)\n"

